Standards-Version: 4.7.0
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: detir-runtime-shared
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 libwayland-client0,
 libwayland-egl1,
 libxkbcommon0,
 libegl1,
 libvulkan1,
 libgl1-mesa-dri,
 mesa-vulkan-drivers,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-base,
 gstreamer1.0-plugins-good,
 gstreamer1.0-libav,
 gstreamer1.0-pulseaudio,
 gstreamer1.0-pipewire,
 pipewire-audio,
 fonts-noto-core | fonts-dejavu-core
Description: Exact-build shared Detir desktop runtime
 The common renderer, event loop and web runtime, with the matched Rust standard
 library in a private ABI-versioned directory. Cerlus and WAID keep separate
 product implementations and processes. Upgrade the matched package set together.

Package: waid-runtime
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, detir-runtime-shared (= ${binary:Version})
Description: WAID app shell over the shared Detir runtime
 The waid-shell executable opens a built app in its own window. Each app has its
 own process and state, using the same installed runtime library as Cerlus.

Package: cerlus
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}, detir-runtime-shared (= ${binary:Version})
Description: Cerlus browser over the shared Detir runtime
 The browser shell, including its own chrome and local agent/workflow product
 code. Browser product code is not part of the shared runtime or WAID.

Package: detir-shell
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 waid-runtime (= ${binary:Version}),
 libwayland-client0,
 libxkbcommon0,
 libegl1,
 labwc (>= 0.9),
 chromium,
 gnome-keyring,
 libpam-gnome-keyring,
 bluez,
 cups,
 cups-browsed,
 avahi-daemon,
 ipp-usb,
 wlr-randr,
 wireplumber,
 xdg-user-dirs,
 dbus-user-session,
 fonts-noto-core | fonts-dejavu-core,
 fonts-dejavu-core
Description: Orus OS shell and Wayland session
 The Orus OS shell (launcher, shell bar, built-in terminal, files, text and
 image apps), the labwc session that hosts it, the orus installer for
 web apps, and System Settings. Registers a Wayland session and unlocks the
 login keyring at console login.

Package: orus-installer
Architecture: all
Depends: ${misc:Depends},
 calamares,
 calamares-settings-debian,
 orus-login,
 waid-runtime,
 sudo
Description: Orus OS graphical installer
 The Calamares installer for Orus OS live media: the installation sequence,
 the runtime license acceptance step, and Orus OS branding. It removes
 itself from the installed system.

Package: orus-login
Architecture: any
Depends: ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends},
 detir-shell,
 greetd,
 labwc (>= 0.9),
 libwayland-client0,
 libxkbcommon0,
 libegl1,
 libvulkan1,
 mesa-vulkan-drivers,
 fonts-noto-core | fonts-dejavu-core
Description: Orus OS graphical login
 A greetd login screen drawn with the Orus OS shell's renderer, running in
 labwc, that starts the Orus OS session. The password typed here goes through
 PAM, so the login keyring unlocks as it does at the console. Install it only
 on machines that should boot to the Orus OS login.
